{"author":{"id":"f943aa1c5ee078b881a8e97535a4e2ccb401d01ca00f4128126befa9cca58a32"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792492627,"nonce":"AOrLvgQgZcBpHp3Ewy/BCFWC/wQ=","title":"release: enable it from the Releases page in one click, the config inferred","message":"Raised while releasing v0.8.0 (2026-10-20). That release was made by hand (tag, `make dist`, `gh release create`), because setting up the Releases page still means editing `.git-board.toml`'s `[release]` table by hand.\n\n**Want:** click and go. The Releases page offers each kind of release with an Enable button, and fills the config itself:\n\n- **Enable web app release**: discovers the images (Dockerfiles), the chart (`helm/`) and the config repo. It infers the registry from the remote in `.git/config`, e.g. `ghcr.io/\u003cowner\u003e/\u003crepo\u003e/\u003cimage\u003e`. The page shows what it found and the user confirms.\n- **Enable binary release**: per-platform archives and checksums attached to the forge's release, what `make dist` + `gh release create` do for git-board itself.\n- **Others**: libraries published to a package registry, and versioned code or scripts, where the tag is the release (see GB-18).\n\n**Done when:** a repo with no `[release]` table gets a working release setup from the Releases page without opening the TOML editor, and git-board's own next release is cut from it.\n\nRelated: GB-18 (kinds of release beyond images and a chart), GB-17 (the pipeline).\n","files":null}]}